# Backend Rules (Custom Structure - Express + Mongoose)

## Architecture (Based on Existing Project)

* Use current structure:
  controllers → services → models → utils/helper
* Keep `crudOperations.js` as reusable data layer
* Controllers handle req/res only
* Services must call crudOperations or custom logic

## Skill Usage (MANDATORY)

* Use `.cursor/skills/use_crud_operations/SKILL.md` when creating new CRUD modules/endpoints
* Use `.cursor/skills/optimize_crud/skill.md` when improving existing CRUD performance/safety
* Use `.cursor/skills/safe_query/skill.md` when implementing/reviewing dynamic filters (for example, getByField)

## Agent Usage

* Use `.cursor/agents/performance_agent.md` for deeper backend performance passes
* Apply this agent after baseline CRUD generation when optimization is requested

## CRUD Strategy

* Use `crudOperations` for basic APIs
* Extend via services for complex logic
* Never duplicate CRUD logic

## Performance (MANDATORY)

* Always use `.lean()` in read queries
* Add pagination:

  * page
  * limit
* Use `.select()` to limit fields
* Avoid full collection fetch

## Response Format

Always return:
```js
{
  success: true,
  message: string,
  data: any,
  meta?: {
    page,
    limit,
    total
  }
}
```

## Error Handling

* Use `http-errors`
* Centralized error middleware
* No raw error exposure

## Validation

* Use `express-validator`
* Validate all inputs
* Reject unknown/unsafe query fields in dynamic filter endpoints

## Security

* Sanitize query params (important for getByField)
* Prevent Mongo injection
* Validate ObjectId before query
* Do not pass raw `req.query` directly to Mongoose filters
* Use field whitelisting for dynamic query APIs

## Logging

* Replace console.log with logger (future improvement)

## File Usage Rules

* controllers → only request/response
* services → business logic
* crudOperations → DB abstraction
* models → schema only

## IMPORTANT

* Do NOT directly use Mongoose in controllers
* Always go through service or crudOperations
